d more experience with  the language  so i'm observing the language now  you do need some grammar  concept you need to be aware of what's a  verb what's a noun what's an adjective  you know uh but many of the things that  happen in the language i'm able to  observe  without having to have it explained to  me without having to  try to remember  explanations i know  uh the word order because i've now seen  so many words and phrases and you'll see  in the overview of how i study that i  say words and phrases i save them as i'm  reading i  tend to go through the lesson sentence  by sentence and then i'll save a word  and a phrase and then i review them  and later on which i don't show you i  can review them in a sort of srs  field if i want so i'm constantly  reviewing words and phrases i'm seeing  the language live in front of me i'm  observing how the language works i'm  observing how concepts are expressed  word order how questions are asked how  adjectives and adverbs behave  and at some point  when i've had enough  of this observing  then i will go and read the explanations  and that'll probably  move my understanding of arabic grammar  you know along  but every time i go there at least at  this stage and i encounter these  theoretical explanations about the  language  about some things that i have already  observed about some things that it's  it's just too difficult for me to relate  the explanation to anything  and i withdraw and i come back to my  observing of the language so my  recommendation and this was my  you know when i first started learning  russian i did it primarily to prove that  to learn a language even a language with  complicated grammar like russian and  arabic has complicated grammar that we  can go a long way without having to  confront the rules and the explanations  and the exceptions we can go a long way  just by observing  and listening reading getting used to  the language and at some point and  certainly more than once  uh later on we can go back in there for  some  explanations but it shouldn't  the sort of upfront grammar explanations  shouldn't prevent us  from enjoying the language and i am  certainly not allowing it to in to you  know  disrupt my enjoyment of arabic where i  feel that i'm making fairly good  progress thank you for listening  bye  so here you can sort of look over my  shoulder  as i work on my ipad  bear in mind that the sentence view  is not yet available on the ipad for the  general user i have a beta version it is  available on the website  the browser version where you go down  and in the settings you can set your  lesson page into different formats  but it will very soon be available uh  for everyone  uh but i just want to use this to  demonstrate how i  mine if you want how i  uh use the text to observe grammar  rather than trying to study it up front  just thought i would give you a  view over my shoulder  bye for now  uber  be  foreign  a  [Music]  you
 

